1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,820
A bow pulled back.

2
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:03,190
A wound-up toy car.

3
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:04,925
A rock at a cliff edge.

4
00:00:05,325 --> 00:00:06,950
None of them is moving.

5
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:09,856
Yet each one is ready
to make something move.

6
00:00:10,306 --> 00:00:13,348
Diya holds a stretched
catapult, perfectly still.

7
00:00:13,348 --> 00:00:16,702
On the roof, a full water
tank sits perfectly still.

8
00:00:17,052 --> 00:00:19,168
Let go, and the stone flies.

9
00:00:19,168 --> 00:00:21,335
Open a tap, and water gushes.

10
00:00:21,335 --> 00:00:22,930
Where was that energy?

11
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:24,495
It was stored.

12
00:00:24,495 --> 00:00:27,876
Today we meet the energy
that waits: potential energy.

13
00:00:28,526 --> 00:00:30,391
So what is potential energy?

14
00:00:30,741 --> 00:00:35,433
It is energy stored because of where
a body is, or the shape it is in.

15
00:00:35,833 --> 00:00:38,642
The tank stores it by
its position, high up.

16
00:00:38,642 --> 00:00:41,534
The catapult stores it
by its shape, stretched.

17
00:00:41,934 --> 00:00:43,434
Potential means possible.

18
00:00:43,434 --> 00:00:47,124
The energy is not moving yet,
but it can come out as motion.

19
00:00:47,524 --> 00:00:51,752
Its symbol is U, and like all
energy, it is measured in joules.

20
00:00:52,402 --> 00:00:53,715
Let's run Diya's catapult.

21
00:00:53,715 --> 00:00:56,955
The band behaves like a spring
of two hundred newtons per metre.

22
00:00:57,305 --> 00:01:00,208
She pulls the pouch back
slowly, twenty centimetres.

23
00:01:00,208 --> 00:01:03,297
The band pulls harder and
harder, up to forty newtons.

24
00:01:03,697 --> 00:01:06,231
Her hand does work against the band.

25
00:01:06,231 --> 00:01:09,033
That work is stored as U: four joules.

26
00:01:09,433 --> 00:01:10,392
She lets go.

27
00:01:10,392 --> 00:01:14,704
The band pulls the eighty gram stone
forward, and the stone flies off.

28
00:01:15,104 --> 00:01:17,681
Slow-mo replay, a hundred times slower.

29
00:01:18,031 --> 00:01:21,093
Now the band's force and the
motion point the same way.

30
00:01:21,093 --> 00:01:22,747
The band does positive work.

31
00:01:23,147 --> 00:01:27,727
As the band shortens, U drains away,
and the stone's kinetic energy grows.

32
00:01:28,127 --> 00:01:31,456
At the end, U is zero,
and K is four joules.

33
00:01:31,456 --> 00:01:34,303
The stone leaves at ten metres per second.

34
00:01:34,953 --> 00:01:37,604
So a force can fill U, or empty it.

35
00:01:37,604 --> 00:01:38,689
Side by side.

36
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:40,189
Lifting a ball.

37
00:01:40,189 --> 00:01:42,793
Gravity pulls down, the ball moves up.

38
00:01:42,793 --> 00:01:45,651
Gravity does negative work, and U goes up.

39
00:01:46,051 --> 00:01:47,360
Dropping the ball.

40
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:50,086
Gravity pulls down, the ball moves down.

41
00:01:50,086 --> 00:01:53,068
Gravity does positive
work, and U goes down.

42
00:01:53,668 --> 00:01:54,700
Now you try.

43
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:55,881
A falling ball.

44
00:01:55,881 --> 00:01:58,875
Gravity does plus five
joules of work on it.

45
00:01:58,875 --> 00:02:01,728
Does U go up or down, and by how much?

46
00:02:01,728 --> 00:02:03,010
Pause and decide.

47
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:07,847
Down, by five joules!

48
00:02:07,847 --> 00:02:10,523
The force's work comes out of the store.

49
00:02:10,523 --> 00:02:12,220
W equals minus delta U.

50
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:14,962
Now the rule, one step at a time.

51
00:02:15,312 --> 00:02:16,212
Step one.

52
00:02:16,173 --> 00:02:20,056
To fill the store slowly,
your push balances the force.

53
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:21,788
Your force is minus F.

54
00:02:22,538 --> 00:02:23,438
Step two.

55
00:02:23,414 --> 00:02:25,007
Your work is stored.

56
00:02:25,007 --> 00:02:28,439
So delta U equals minus
the integral of F d x.

57
00:02:29,189 --> 00:02:30,203
Step three.

58
00:02:30,203 --> 00:02:33,633
For one tiny step, d U equals minus F d x.

59
00:02:34,383 --> 00:02:35,380
Step four.

60
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:36,744
Divide by d x.

61
00:02:36,744 --> 00:02:39,072
F equals minus d U by d x.

62
00:02:39,822 --> 00:02:42,404
Check with gravity, up positive.

63
00:02:42,404 --> 00:02:47,570
U equals m g h, so d U by d
h is m g, and F is minus m g.

64
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:48,500
Downwards.

65
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,441
It works.

66
00:02:50,191 --> 00:02:51,195
Remember this.

67
00:02:51,195 --> 00:02:53,474
The force is minus the slope of U.

68
00:02:53,474 --> 00:02:55,547
It always pushes toward lower U.

69
00:02:56,247 --> 00:02:57,636
Why the minus sign?

70
00:02:57,636 --> 00:02:58,870
Follow the links.

71
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,120
One.

72
00:02:59,769 --> 00:03:03,591
Where U rises as x increases,
the slope is positive.

73
00:03:03,991 --> 00:03:04,891
Two.

74
00:03:04,430 --> 00:03:06,640
The minus sign makes F negative there.

75
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:08,937
The force points back, toward lower U.

76
00:03:09,337 --> 00:03:10,237
Three.

77
00:03:09,937 --> 00:03:12,980
Where U falls as x
increases, F is positive.

78
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:14,497
Again toward lower U.

79
00:03:14,897 --> 00:03:15,797
Four.

80
00:03:15,415 --> 00:03:18,225
Where the slope is
flat, the force is zero.

81
00:03:18,225 --> 00:03:21,044
Like a ball resting at
the bottom of a bowl.

82
00:03:21,644 --> 00:03:22,544
Your turn.

83
00:03:22,544 --> 00:03:26,495
On a U against x graph, U
drops steeply as x increases.

84
00:03:26,495 --> 00:03:28,729
Which way does the force point?

85
00:03:28,729 --> 00:03:30,001
Pause and think.

86
00:03:33,201 --> 00:03:34,240
Along plus x!

87
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,375
Toward lower U.

88
00:03:35,375 --> 00:03:37,550
And steeper means a bigger force.

89
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:39,890
Now, one worked example.

90
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:44,363
A particle has U equals three x
squared minus twelve x joules.

91
00:03:44,363 --> 00:03:48,335
Find the force at one metre,
and where the force is zero.

92
00:03:48,835 --> 00:03:51,036
F is minus d U by d x.

93
00:03:51,036 --> 00:03:54,043
d U by d x is six x minus twelve.

94
00:03:54,793 --> 00:03:57,258
So F equals twelve minus six x.

95
00:03:58,008 --> 00:04:02,338
At one metre, F is twelve minus
six, six newtons, along plus x.

96
00:04:03,088 --> 00:04:05,543
F is zero when six x equals twelve.

97
00:04:05,543 --> 00:04:08,453
At two metres, the bottom of the U curve.

98
00:04:09,103 --> 00:04:10,565
Now, the exam trap.

99
00:04:10,915 --> 00:04:13,060
Many students drop the minus sign.

100
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:16,858
They write F equals d U by d
x, and get minus six newtons.

101
00:04:17,258 --> 00:04:19,815
But the force points toward lower U.

102
00:04:19,815 --> 00:04:23,356
Keep the minus sign: F
equals minus d U by d x.

103
00:04:24,006 --> 00:04:25,302
Where is this asked?

104
00:04:25,302 --> 00:04:29,353
In questions that give U as a formula
or a graph, and ask for the force

105
00:04:29,353 --> 00:04:30,253
or the work.

106
00:04:30,849 --> 00:04:32,092
Exam level now.

107
00:04:32,092 --> 00:04:34,917
U equals x squared minus four x joules.

108
00:04:34,917 --> 00:04:39,048
A particle moves from x equals
one to x equals four metres.

109
00:04:39,048 --> 00:04:43,507
Find the work done by the force,
and the force at four metres.

110
00:04:43,507 --> 00:04:44,803
Pause and solve.

111
00:04:50,203 --> 00:04:51,341
The answer is A.

112
00:04:51,341 --> 00:04:53,918
Minus three joules,
and minus four newtons.

113
00:04:54,418 --> 00:04:58,253
U at one metre is minus
three, at four metres zero.

114
00:04:58,253 --> 00:05:00,257
So delta U is plus three.

115
00:05:00,757 --> 00:05:03,471
Work by the force is minus delta U.

116
00:05:03,471 --> 00:05:04,981
Minus three joules.

117
00:05:05,481 --> 00:05:08,987
F is minus d U by d x,
minus two x plus four.

118
00:05:08,987 --> 00:05:11,539
At four metres, minus four newtons.

119
00:05:12,139 --> 00:05:13,679
Here is your recap.

120
00:05:13,679 --> 00:05:15,261
Screenshot this card.

121
00:05:18,461 --> 00:05:20,400
Can you answer these without help?

122
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,700
One.

123
00:05:21,206 --> 00:05:24,486
Where is the energy in a stretched
catapult that is not moving?

124
00:05:25,386 --> 00:05:26,286
Two.

125
00:05:25,849 --> 00:05:28,890
Gravity does ten joules
of work on a falling ball.

126
00:05:28,890 --> 00:05:30,387
What happens to its U?

127
00:05:31,287 --> 00:05:32,187
Three.

128
00:05:31,883 --> 00:05:35,583
Why does F equals minus d U
by d x carry a minus sign?

129
00:05:36,683 --> 00:05:40,534
Next time: water from a rooftop
tank gushes out of a tap.

130
00:05:40,534 --> 00:05:42,961
How much energy does height give it?

131
00:05:42,961 --> 00:05:44,906
Gravitational potential energy.
